{"uid":"headers/drivers/usbhid.h::usbhid_set1_from_usage","name":"usbhid_set1_from_usage","qualname":"usbhid_set1_from_usage","kind":"function","file":"headers/drivers/usbhid.h","line":127,"end_line":127,"language":"h","signature":"int usbhid_set1_from_usage(unsigned usage, unsigned char *sc, int *e0);","params":[{"name":"usage","annotation":"unsigned","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"sc","annotation":"unsigned char *","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"e0","annotation":"int *","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"int","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Docstring: Translate a HID usage code to its PS/2 set-1 make code and whether it needs the 0xE0 prefix.","description":"Returns 0 for a usage with no set-1 equivalent, which the caller drops rather than inventing a scancode for.\n\nA pure function over a table, host-testable: HID usage ids are not\nscancodes above 0x27 (usage 0x28 is Return while set-1 Return is 0x1C), and\nthe navigation cluster and the right-hand modifiers exist in one place on\na USB keyboard while set-1 needs the prefix to tell them from their\nleft-hand twins. Both decisions live here so no caller has to know them.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"headers/drivers/usbhid.h","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
